CAT = "jelecEquip"; SEG = "EQP"
Q = [
("Flexible cords and cables are not permitted:",
 "As a substitute for fixed wiring", ["For portable lamps", "For pendant luminaires", "For connecting appliances"],
 "Flexible cords may not be used as a substitute for the fixed wiring of a structure, run through holes in walls or ceilings, or concealed behind walls. Pendants, portable lamps and appliance connections are permitted uses."),
("Where must 15 A and 20 A, 125 V receptacles be tamper-resistant?",
 "Throughout dwelling units", ["Only in children's bedrooms", "Only in kitchens", "Only near floor level"],
 "Nonlocking 15 A and 20 A, 125 V and 250 V receptacles in all areas of dwelling units must be listed tamper-resistant, with limited exceptions such as receptacles more than 5 1/2 ft above the floor."),
("A 15 A or 20 A receptacle in a wet location must have an enclosure that is:",
 "Weatherproof with a plug inserted", ["Weatherproof only when closed", "Raintight only when unused", "Rated for damp locations"],
 "Outdoor 15 A and 20 A, 125 and 250 V receptacles in wet locations need an extra-duty in-use cover that is weatherproof whether or not a plug is inserted."),
("Which receptacle installation is prohibited?",
 "Face-up in a countertop", ["On a garage wall", "Behind a refrigerator", "In a weatherproof box outdoors"],
 "Receptacles may not be installed in a face-up position in countertops or similar work surfaces, where spills can enter them. Listed pop-up assemblies are the exception."),
("Where no equipment ground exists, a nongrounding receptacle may be replaced with:",
 "A GFCI-type receptacle", ["A grounding receptacle alone", "A 20 A grounding receptacle", "An isolated-ground receptacle"],
 "A nongrounding receptacle may be replaced with another nongrounding one, a GFCI receptacle marked \"No Equipment Ground\", or a grounding receptacle protected by a GFCI and marked accordingly."),
("Three-way and four-way switches must be wired so that all switching is done in:",
 "The ungrounded conductor", ["The grounded conductor", "The grounding conductor", "Both circuit conductors"],
 "Switches must open the ungrounded conductor. Switching the neutral would leave the luminaire energized when it appears to be off."),
("A permanently connected appliance rated over 300 VA needs a disconnecting means that is:",
 "Within sight or lockable", ["Within 6 ft of the panel", "A cord and plug only", "Inside the appliance"],
 "For permanently connected appliances over 300 VA, the branch-circuit switch or breaker may serve as the disconnect if it is within sight of the appliance or can be locked in the open position."),
("A panelboard circuit directory entry is not acceptable if it depends on:",
 "Who occupies the room", ["The room's permanent use", "The equipment served", "The circuit's location"],
 "Each circuit must be legibly identified as to its clear, evident and specific purpose. The description may not depend on transient conditions of occupancy, such as a tenant's name."),
("No hanging luminaires or ceiling fans may be within a zone measured from a bathtub rim. How far does it extend?",
 "3 ft out, 8 ft up", ["2 ft out, 6 ft up", "3 ft out, 6 ft up", "6 ft out, 8 ft up"],
 "No cord-connected, chain-, cable- or cord-suspended luminaires, track lighting, pendants or ceiling fans may be within 3 ft horizontally and 8 ft vertically from the top of the bathtub rim or shower threshold."),
("A garbage disposer supplied by a flexible cord must use a cord between:",
 "18 and 36 in. long", ["3 and 6 1/2 ft long", "6 and 12 in. long", "36 and 48 in. long"],
 "In-sink waste disposers may be cord connected with a cord 18 to 36 in. long, terminated in a grounding-type plug. Dishwashers use a longer cord."),
("Which luminaire is not permitted in a clothes closet?",
 "Open-lamp incandescent", ["Surface LED, enclosed lamp", "Recessed LED", "Surface fluorescent"],
 "Incandescent luminaires with open or partially enclosed lamps, and pendants, may not be installed in clothes closets. Enclosed LED, fluorescent and incandescent types are allowed with set clearances."),
("Unless marked for more, an outlet box designed to support a luminaire may carry a luminaire weighing up to:",
 "50 lb", ["35 lb", "70 lb", "25 lb"],
 "Boxes for luminaire support must support at least 50 lb. A heavier luminaire must be supported independently unless the box is listed and marked for that weight."),
("Outlet boxes used as the sole support of a ceiling-suspended fan must be:",
 "Listed for fan support", ["Rated for 50 lb or more", "Made of metal only", "At least 2 1/8 in. deep"],
 "Boxes that are the sole support of a ceiling fan must be listed and marked as suitable for fan support, and fans over 35 lb need the box marked with the maximum weight."),
("A built-in dishwasher supplied by a flexible cord must use a cord between:",
 "3 and 6 1/2 ft long", ["18 and 36 in. long", "2 and 4 ft long", "6 and 10 ft long"],
 "Built-in dishwashers and trash compactors may be cord connected with a cord at least 3 ft and not more than 6 1/2 ft long, measured from the face of the attachment plug."),
("Why does the NEC require a grounded conductor at most lighting switch locations?",
 "To supply electronic controls", ["To ground the switch yoke", "To allow neutral switching", "To serve as a traveler"],
 "A grounded conductor is required at most switch locations so occupancy sensors, timers and other electronic switches can be installed without sending current on the equipment ground."),
("With primary-only protection, a transformer of 1000 V or less with a primary current of 9 A or more may be protected at no more than:",
 "125 percent", ["150 percent", "250 percent", "300 percent"],
 "Primary-only protection for transformers of 1000 V or less is set at 125 percent of rated primary current where it is 9 A or more, with the next higher standard size allowed."),
]
